[[:db/cas 17592186197769 :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - t, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" "\\left\\langle e^{t} - t, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186197770 :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" "\\left\\langle e^{t}, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186197771 :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" "\\left\\langle e^{t}, \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186197772 :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩" "\\left\\langle e^{t}, \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186197773 :answer/value "⟨e^{t} - t, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩" "\\left\\langle e^{t} - t, \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186319191 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186319368 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle -\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332819 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186330808 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186330907 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186330933 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186331142 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186331814 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186332820 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={\\sin }^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={\\cos }^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={\\sin }^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\sin }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=3{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={\\cos }^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\left\\langle {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186330507 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186330861 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186330866 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186330966 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186331226 :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" "\\sqrt{2}\\left\\langle \\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186332821 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{\\sec }^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\left\\langle {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186330790 :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" "\\sqrt{2}\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186392722 :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}\\right\\rangle ,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$"] [:db/cas 17592186392722 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392724 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186392725 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186392726 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186392727 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186392728 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186501155 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186500478 :answer/value "⟨4t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle 4t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186500627 :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{3t}⟩" "\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{1}{3t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186500681 :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle 4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186500932 :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186541128 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n* For the $x$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=\\frac{5}{25+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n* For the $y$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=(\\sqrt{5})^{2}-2=3.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}),{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{6},3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n* For the $x$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=\\frac{5}{25+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n* For the $y$-component, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})=(\\sqrt{5})^{2}-2=3.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}),{y}^{′}(\\sqrt{5})⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{6},3\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186578791 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=(t-1)({t}^{2}+2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(1)({t}^{2}+2)+(t-1)(2t) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)+2t(t-1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=({(-1)}^{2}+2)+2(-1)((-1)-1)=7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8-{t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{2t}{8-{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{8-{(-1)}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,\\,\\frac{2}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=(t-1)({t}^{2}+2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(1)({t}^{2}+2)+(t-1)(2t) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)+2t(t-1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=({(-1)}^{2}+2)+2(-1)((-1)-1)=7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8-{t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{2t}{8-{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{8-{(-1)}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 7,\\,\\frac{2}{7}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186578857 :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t),\\,\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(2)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(2)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle 12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t),\\,\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}\\right\\rangle ,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(2)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(2)|=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186708402 :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= \\ln{\\left(t^{2} - 4 \\right)} \\\\ x'(t) &= \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= 2 e^{3 t} \\\\ y'(t) &= 6 e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\rangle\n$$" "For the $x$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= \\ln{\\left(t^{2} - 4 \\right)} \\\\ x'(t) &= \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= 2 e^{3 t} \\\\ y'(t) &= 6 e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186708414 :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{1}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\rangle" "\\left\\langle \\frac{1}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708415 :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\rangle" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 6 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708416 :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 0\\rangle" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 0\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708424 :answer/value "\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 2 e^{3 t}\\rangle" "\\left\\langle \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} - 4},\\, 2 e^{3 t}\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708409 :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - 6 \\sqrt{t} \\\\ x'(t) &= - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= e^{2 t} - 4 \\\\ y'(t) &= 2 e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\langle - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}},\\, 2 e^{2 t}\\rangle\n$$" "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= - 6 \\sqrt{t} \\\\ x'(t) &= - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= e^{2 t} - 4 \\\\ y'(t) &= 2 e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}},\\, 2 e^{2 t}\\right\\rangle\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186708417 :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\langle t^{6},\\, \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?" "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle t^{6},\\, \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\right\\rangle$, what is $r'(t)$?"] [:db/cas 17592186708417 :question/worked-solution "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= t^{6} \\\\ x'(t) &= 6 t^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the quotient and chain rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2} \\\\ y'(t) &= \\frac{(2 e^{2 t})(e^{2 t} + 2)-(e^{2 t})(2 e^{2 t})}{(e^{2 t} + 2)^2} \\\\ &= \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\rangle\n$$" "For the $x$-component, use the power rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) &= t^{6} \\\\ x'(t) &= 6 t^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-component, use the quotient and chain rules.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) &= \\frac{e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2} \\\\ y'(t) &= \\frac{(2 e^{2 t})(e^{2 t} + 2)-(e^{2 t})(2 e^{2 t})}{(e^{2 t} + 2)^2} \\\\ &= \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the coordinate order:\n\n$$\nr'(t)=\\left\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186708399 :answer/value "\\langle 6 t,\\, \\frac{2 \\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right) e^{2 t} + 2 e^{4 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\rangle" "\\left\\langle 6 t,\\, \\frac{2 \\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right) e^{2 t} + 2 e^{4 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708403 :answer/value "\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\rangle" "\\left\\langle 6 t^{5},\\, \\frac{4 e^{2 t}}{\\left(e^{2 t} + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle"] [:db/cas 17592186708418 :answer/value "\\langle t^{5},\\, \\frac{2 e^{2 t}}{e^{2 t} + 2}\\rangle" "\\lef