{t^{2} - 1},-25\\cos (5t)\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186259484 :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186257689 :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186257727 :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({\\cot }^{2}⁡t+{\\csc }^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" "\\left\\langle \\operat