igned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\left\\langle -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\\right\\rangle \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186388106 :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" "\\left\\langle 1,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186388107 :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" "\\left\\langle 0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186388109 :answer/value "⟨2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi -2)⟩" "\\left\\langle 2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi -2)\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186388110 :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2\\pi ⟩" "\\left\\langle 0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2\\pi \\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186501172 :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186578797 :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡4t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6(t+5)^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(14-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+60,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡4t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6(t+5)^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(14-t)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+60,-1\\right\\rangle \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186578313 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+60,-1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+60,-1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186578343 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{1+4{t}^{2}},12t+6,-1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+4{t}^{2}},12t+6,-1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186578410 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+5,-1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+5,-1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186578530 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+6,1⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+6,1\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186578626 :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},10t+30,14⟩" "\\left\\langle \\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},10t+30,14\\right\\rangle "] [:db/cas 17592186578882 :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi ),$ we substitute $t=\\pi$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi ),$ we substitute $t=\\pi$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186198227 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\left\\langle \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,1\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1\\right\\rangle \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186199448 :tutorial/content "Differentiating vector-valued functions is easy: we just differentiate each component separately. So, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< x(t), \\, y(t) \\right>,\n$$\n\n then \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\mathbf{r} }{\\textrm dt}  = \\mathbf{r}'(t) = \\left< x'(t), \\, y'(t) \\right>.\n$$\n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< t+1, \\, t^2+2 \\right>,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGeometrically, the derivative of a vector-valued function $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t$ gives a vector that's tangent to the curve traced out by $\\mathbf r(t)$ at $t.$\n\n![](images/6d/6d7f1a972197ff5a92bb64bd0bab9e6dd779e800be48232124f8fda39fa3c949.png)\n\nLet's see some examples." "Differentiating vector-valued functions is easy: we just differentiate each component separately. So, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< x(t), \\, y(t) \\right>,\n$$\n\n then \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\mathbf{r} }{\\textrm dt}  = \\mathbf{r}'(t) = \\left< x'(t), \\, y'(t) \\right>.\n$$\n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left< t+1, \\, t^2+2 \\right>,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGeometrically, the derivative of a vector-valued function $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t$ gives a vector that's tangent to the curve traced out by $\\mathbf r(t)$ at $t.$\n\n![](images/6d/6d7f1a972197ff5a92bb64bd0bab9e6dd779e800be48232124f8fda39fa3c949.png)\n\nLet's see some examples."] [:db/cas 17592186199449 :tutorial/content "We can differentiate vector-valued functions with three components in the same way. \n\nFor example, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t) = \\big\\langle x(t), \\: y(t), \\: z(t) \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nis our vector-valued function, then the derivative is computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\text{d}\\mathbf{f}}{\\text{d}t} = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{ \\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, suppose that we are given the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\left\\langle t^3, \\:  \\ln(t+3), \\:  \\sqrt{t}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\n \n\nTo compute the derivative $\\mathbf f'\\!(t),$ we find the derivative of each component function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{d}{dt}⟨{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We can differentiate vector-valued functions with three components in the same way. \n\nFor example, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t) = \\big\\langle x(t), \\: y(t), \\: z(t) \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nis our vector-valued function, then the derivative is computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\text{d}\\mathbf{f}}{\\text{d}t} = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{ \\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, suppose that we are given the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\left\\langle t^3, \\:  \\ln(t+3), \\:  \\sqrt{t}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\n \n\nTo compute the derivative $\\mathbf f'\\!(t),$ we find the derivative of each component function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{d}{dt}⟨{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sqrt{t})\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\right\\rangle \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/ensure 17592186198983 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186319191 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186319368 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186332819 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186332820 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186332821 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186392722 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186501155 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186541128 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186578791 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186578857 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186708402 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186708409 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186708417 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186198230 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186198985 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186259484 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186302156 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186387346 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186393751 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186403794 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186501242 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186578808 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186707802 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186198942 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186265901 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186319193 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186388104 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186501172 :